    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "After weeks of relentless rain, one of the heaviest rainy seasons in three decades pushed the river everyone shares past its limits. Water systems were pushed to their limits, and fast-moving water entered populated and agricultural areas, swamping the everyday places where people live and work in ordinary communities in eastern Syria. Rescue crews on the water worked to get families to safety, but the disaster outcome was tragic with fatalities among children. An upstream neighbor agreeing to help made a practical concession to ease the burden.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Everyman",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "how-0",
          "how-1",
          "how-2",
          "how-3",
